  "title": "The Order-Seven Degree-Square Turan Problem for the Regular Five-Vertex Tournament",
  "batch_label": "65",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "Let D range over all loopless digraphs on seven labeled vertices, with at most one arc in each ordered direction and with antiparallel arcs allowed. If D contains no not-necessarily-induced copy of the regular five-vertex tournament Reg5, then sum_v d_D^+(v)^2 <= 186. Equality is attained, and it holds exactly for the 105 labeled copies of the balanced complete bidirected four-partite graph T_4(7), whose part sizes are 2,2,2,1. Equivalently, ex^+_{L2}(7,Reg5)=186 with this equality classification.",
